llm_user_prompt:
Plain visual read of the image (pixels only — the ground truth for what the scene visibly shows):
${step1Output}

Additional context (human-provided, may be empty):
${imageAdditionalContext}

The image's physical analog (core = the binding relational skeleton; secondary = nice-to-have texture):
${step2Output}

The extracted entities (ensemble figures + secondary non-figure entities):
${step3Output}

Read the image through the INTERNAL lens only (me vs my own brain). Cast EVERY figure and rate every fit.

ALSO, for EACH secondary entity in the extracted entities (there may be none): NOMINATE 1-3 possibilities for what it could be in her world THROUGH THIS LENS — short noun phrases in the same register as this read's entities. THE TEST: each possibility must be recognizable persona-world content a caption could use without pointing at any figure. A secondary entity with no natural counterpart in this lens gets an empty possibilities list — never force one.
RIGHT (form illustration only — never copy): "a high-stakes situation" → "the 3am window where one notification decides my whole night"

Output ONLY strict JSON (placeholders are NOT values; never copy them):
{
  "ensemble": [
    { "figure": "<a figure/side, quoted from the plain visual read>", "entity": "<me / a state-stamped self / ONE canon force>", "fit": <0-1>, "reason": "<one sentence grounded in what the figure visibly does>" }
  ],
  "weakest_fit": <the lowest fit in the ensemble>,
  "why": "<one sentence: the internal dynamic this arrangement plays>",
  "secondary_nominations": [
    { "entity": "<a secondary entity, copied VERBATIM from the extracted entities — empty array if there are none>", "possibilities": ["<1-3 short phrases from her world in this lens>"] }
  ]
}
